From 46d9eb002fcc835cd86575eb018fec8cd969c233 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:17:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Quota intelligence: quotas in words, from a sheet, and
 watched in the field (research intelligence, Phase 4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Quotas were enforced end to end but set up by hand, cell by cell; the copilot
could create one only in the simplest shape. Now "500 completes, 50/50 gender,
interlocked with 18–34 (40%), 35–54 (35%) and 55+" is one create_quota with
dimensions: the engine builds the crossing on the real option codes, splits
the total by largest remainder so the limits add up exactly, and places the
quota check right after the last question the cells read. Explicit cells (a
condition, a count or a percent of the total) still work and mix with them.

Engine (packages/engine/src/quotaActions.ts, new; create_quota moved into it,
the old shape unchanged): update_quota (rename, a new total rescaling every
count cell in proportion, mode, what happens when full — copied onto the
quota's check — cells by label), add_quota_cells (the check moves if the new
cells read a later question), remove_quota_cells and delete_quota
(destructive, confirmed; the check and List Fill references go too),
set_quota_check (after a question or block, with a condition; too early is
said). reviewQuotas — in the survey review, the Quotas tab and the copilot's
outline — finds the groups no cell covers (every answer combination of the
questions the cells read is tried, band edges and their neighbours and the
question's own bounds for numbers), cells matching the same respondent,
limits that do not add up to the total (with the rescale as the fix), percent
cells under 100 or without a total, a zero (unlimited) cell, a quota nothing
checks, a check before its question (critical, with the move as the fix).
quotaAdvice reads the live counts: a full cell while the rest is open, a cell
well under its share of what has come in with the projected shortfall,
nearly full, complete — each adjustment an update_quota to preview. The
Changes lines name added, changed, removed quotas and placed checks. Ranked
after the structure (a quota may read a question created in the same batch).

Import (packages/import/src/quotaSheet.ts, new): a client's Excel/CSV read in
three layouts — long (dimension columns, a target column, Quota/Label
columns, a Total row), matrix (a cross-tab, totals ignored), list — and
mapped against the open survey: headers to questions (code, variable, text,
and decisively the values under them), values to options (several joined
with /) or numeric ranges (18–24, 55+, under 18, 65 and over), targets to
counts or percents; what does not match is reported by row and left out.
sources.ts gained readSheets, the one Excel/CSV reader readSource now uses.

Studio: COPILOT_QUOTA_GUIDE and quotaIntent; on a quota turn the outline
carries every quota's cells, conditions, check position, review findings and
— with the live counts the hook now sends — the counts and advice.
POST /api/import/quotas (file + definition → gated actions, issues, matched
columns). Intelligent → Quotas (QuotasTab): the review with Add/Move the
check and Rescale to the total, each quota's cells and counts with the
advice and its adjustments, Make soft, Ask the copilot, Import a quota
sheet, the last import's matched columns and left-out rows. The attach menu
and the drop choice offer a quota sheet; useCopilot loads quota_counts from
the dashboard's route (and a test seam). One quota system throughout:
def.quotas, quota_check, quota_counts, the dashboard's route.

Tests: engine quotaActions.test.ts (5; 79 mutations, 78 caught, one
equivalent — the follow-up found and fixed a real bug: numeric bounds were
read as settings.min/max instead of minValue/maxValue); import
quotaSheet.test.ts (5; 32/32); studio copilot.test.ts (+1; 8/8); browser
scripts/quota-copilot-test.mjs (9 checks; 11/11 against the Studio
surfaces). Engine 1424, import 28, Studio 222; quota-dashboard, copilot,
analysis-framework, translation-copilot, ux-copilot, intelligent-mode,
import-engine, wave2, e2e-smoke, remaining-items and master-demo browser
suites green (copilot-test's attach-menu expectation gains the new entry).
Docs: docs/QUOTA-INTELLIGENCE-2026-10-04.md.

